<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="t00217">
	<title id="e01345">Adjusting the height up and down </title>
	<taskbody>
		<context>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01346">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e01347">
									<image href="images/N_SP327_B06_024_1.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
		</context>
		<steps>
			<step>
				<cmd>To raise the headrest, pull it up to the desired position.</cmd>
			</step>
			<step>
				<cmd>To lower the headrest:</cmd>
				<substeps>
					<substep>
						<cmd>Push and hold the release button (1) on the headrest support.</cmd>
					</substep>
					<substep>
						<cmd>Lower the headrest to the desired position.</cmd>
					</substep>
				</substeps>
				<info>
					<note type="warning" id="e01348">
						<p>To properly protect the occupants, make sure the headrest locks in position after adjusting it.</p>
					</note>
					<note type="caution" id="e01349">
						<p>If you angle the seatback forward with the headrest and seat cushion raised, the headrest may contact the sun visor or other parts of the vehicle.</p>
						<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01350">
							<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
								<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
								<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
								<tbody>
									<row rowsep="1">
										<entry colname="col1">
											<fig id="e01351">
												<image href="images/N_SP3i26_D06_030_E.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
											</fig>
										</entry>
										<entry colname="col2"/>
									</row>
								</tbody>
							</tgroup>
						</table>
					</note>
				</info>
			</step>
		</steps>
	</taskbody>
